INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(209,'https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/1012438/hollywood-tech-backlash-you-can-see-everything-musk-the-social-reckoning-artificial','https://theverge.com/entertainment/1012438/hollywood-tech-backlash-you-can-see-everything-musk-the-social-reckoning-artificial','The tech backlash is now in theaters','thetechbacklashisnowintheaters','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-10-15T21:39:52Z','2026-10-17T08:44:23Z','Though movies about disruptive tech founders are nothing new, 2026 has been unusually stacked with features that take a much more critical look at how Silicon Valley is reshaping our reality. Aaron Sorkin''s The Social Reckoning frames Mark Zuckerberg as a robotic villain whose ambitions are destabilizing society. Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim''s You Can […]',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(210,'https://www.theverge.com/policy/1012445/donald-trump-ai-photo-white-house-rennovation-column','https://theverge.com/policy/1012445/donald-trump-ai-photo-white-house-rennovation-column','Trump posts AI-edited photo to brag about White House restoration work','trumppostsaieditedphototobragaboutwhitehouserestorationwork','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-10-15T21:09:33Z','2026-10-17T08:44:23Z','President Donald Trump posted a series of photos on Truth Social showing off renovations to the White House - but one of them appears to be modified with AI. The picture, which compares an old White House column to a "restored" one, has several discrepancies and was flagged by Google''s AI detector as "made or […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(211,'https://www.theverge.com/tech/1012374/bluesky-ai-attie-small-social-games-apps','https://theverge.com/tech/1012374/bluesky-ai-attie-small-social-games-apps','Bluesky’s AI tool now lets you make games and apps to share on social','blueskysaitoolnowletsyoumakegamesandappstoshareonsocial','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-10-15T19:57:16Z','2026-10-17T08:44:23Z','Bluesky''s Attie AI tool, which initially launched earlier this year as a way to use AI to build your own feeds, now lets you make "small" social apps like games, polls, and dashboards that you can then share with others as their own websites. In an interview at TechCrunch Disrupt, Bluesky CEO Toni Schneider said […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
