INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(215,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/doe-selects-38-research-projects-for-36m-in-epscor-funding/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/doe-selects-38-research-projects-for-36m-in-epscor-funding','DOE Selects 38 Research Projects for $36M in EPSCoR Funding','doeselects38researchprojectsfor36minepscorfunding','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-10-16T21:59:51Z','2026-10-17T08:44:24Z','WASHINGTON, Oct. 16, 2026 — The U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) today announced the selection of 38 research projects in 21 states and Puerto Rico to receive a combined $36 million through the Established Program to Stimulate Competitive Research (EPSCoR). These projects will empower the next generation of American researchers in historically underfunded regions to pursue groundbreaking […] The post DOE Selects 38 Research Projects for $36M in EPSCoR Funding appeared first on HPCwire .',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(216,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/giga-computing-powers-scaleways-new-amd-instinct-gpu-services-to-accelerate-ai-workloads/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/giga-computing-powers-scaleways-new-amd-instinct-gpu-services-to-accelerate-ai-workloads','Giga Computing Powers Scaleway’s New AMD Instinct GPU Services to Accelerate AI Workloads','gigacomputingpowersscalewaysnewamdinstinctgpuservicestoaccelerateaiworkloads','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-10-16T21:49:16Z','2026-10-17T08:44:24Z','Oct. 16, 2026 — Giga Computing, a subsidiary of GIGABYTE and a leader in advanced cooling servers and infrastructure solutions, has announced its collaboration with Scaleway on the launch of AI and cloud platforms using AMD Instinct GPUs, unveiled at ai-PULSE in Paris. Giga Computing provides the servers at the heart of the compute infrastructure, […] The post Giga Computing Powers Scaleway’s New AMD Instinct GPU Services to Accelerate AI Workloads appeared first on HPCwire .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(217,'https://www.hpcwire.com/2026/10/16/from-curiosity-to-compute-creating-new-pathways-into-hpc/','https://hpcwire.com/2026/10/16/from-curiosity-to-compute-creating-new-pathways-into-hpc','From Curiosity to Compute: Creating New Pathways into HPC','fromcuriositytocomputecreatingnewpathwaysintohpc','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-10-16T19:25:05Z','2026-10-17T08:44:24Z','At University College London (UCL), a group of students applauded when a small supercomputer switched on. To be fair, they’d just helped assemble it. We’d handed out cables, invited people to connect the components and encouraged questions. Why did that cable go into this port? What was the difference between Ethernet and Omni-Path? How did […] The post From Curiosity to Compute: Creating New Pathways into HPC appeared first on HPCwire .',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(218,'https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/ericsson-and-partners-launch-sferical-one-ai-supercomputer-in-sweden/','https://hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/ericsson-and-partners-launch-sferical-one-ai-supercomputer-in-sweden','Ericsson and Partners Launch Sferical One AI Supercomputer in Sweden','ericssonandpartnerslaunchsfericaloneaisupercomputerinsweden','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-10-16T17:50:32Z','2026-10-17T08:44:24Z','Oct. 16, 2026 — Ericsson is among several major Swedish companies who have started to utilize a new sovereign AI supercomputer in Sweden, called Sferical One, officially launched this week by the Sferical AI initiative. As a founding member of Sferical AI – alongside AstraZeneca, Saab, SEB and Wallenberg Investments, with SKF as a strategic partner […] The post Ericsson and Partners Launch Sferical One AI Supercomputer in Sweden appeared first on HPCwire .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
