INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(1340,'https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1013643/ai-agents-hack-john-deere-shark-ninja-cummins','https://theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1013643/ai-agents-hack-john-deere-shark-ninja-cummins','A hacker broke into John Deere and SharkNinja with an army of AI agents','ahackerbrokeintojohndeereandsharkninjawithanarmyofaiagents','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-10-19T13:58:41Z','2026-10-20T03:02:27Z','A hacker broke into more than 100 websites using an army of AI agents that mostly operated on their own, according to findings from the AI security firm Norforge. Though Norforge doesn''t name the targets, Reuters reports that the victims included companies like John Deere, SharkNinja, and Cummins. Concerns over AI-powered cybersecurity breaches have grown […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(1341,'https://www.theverge.com/policy/1013113/democrats-ai-midterms','https://theverge.com/policy/1013113/democrats-ai-midterms','Democrats think cracking down on AI could give them an edge','democratsthinkcrackingdownonaicouldgivethemanedge','theverge_ai','The Verge - AI','en','2026-10-19T12:00:00Z','2026-10-20T03:02:27Z','Democrats could win back control of Congress this November, and if they do, they''ll need to decide how to approach one of the country''s newest and thorniest political issues: AI. Polls predict Democrats will flip at least one chamber of Congress in the midterm elections, which would put committee leadership back in their hands. That […]',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(1342,'https://www.hpcwire.com/2026/10/19/quantinuum-says-helios-results-strengthen-its-path-to-apollo/','https://hpcwire.com/2026/10/19/quantinuum-says-helios-results-strengthen-its-path-to-apollo','Quantinuum Says Helios Results Strengthen Its Path to Apollo','quantinuumsaysheliosresultsstrengthenitspathtoapollo','hpcwire','HPCwire','en','2026-10-19T22:54:52Z','2026-10-20T03:02:28Z','Quantinuum says a new error-correction result on its Helios quantum computer gives it greater confidence in a 2029 target for Apollo, its planned fault-tolerant system. The company reported 99.9995% logical memory fidelity, equivalent to roughly five failures per million cycles. “This derisks the industry,” Quantinuum CEO Rajeeb Hazra told The Wall Street Journal. “We now […] The post Quantinuum Says Helios Results Strengthen Its Path to Apollo appeared first on HPCwire .',0.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
